  "title": "Wavelet Fine-Tuning and SDS-LoRA: Efficient and Robust Parameter Adaptation in Vision",
  "summary": "WaveFT efficiently adapts large pretrained models using sparse updates in the wavelet domain, while SDS-LoRA introduces a geometrically decoupled low-rank parameterization to overcome anisotropic gradient scaling. Both methods improve performance by preserving the full gradient structure and reducing the adaptation gap.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "WaveFT learns sparse updates in the wavelet domain, enabling fine-grained control over trainable parameters.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "WaveFT demonstrates state-of-the-art results in vision tasks, showing improved gradient coverage and performance compared to SHiRA.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SDS-LoRA addresses anisotropic scaling by structurally decoupling the singular values from the backward pass, improving convergence and adaptation performance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
